1.4.5 Landfilling
WARM considers the CH4 emissions, transportation-related CO2 emissions and carbon storage that will result from landfilling each type of organic waste and mixed MSW. Because glass is not an organic material, it does not generate CH4 or sequester any carbon when landfilled. The only emissions associated with landfilling glass are those from transporting glass to the landfills and moving waste around in the landfills. Transportation of waste materials results in anthropogenic CO2 emissions due to the combustion of fossil fuels in the vehicles used to haul the wastes. For further information, please refer to the chapter on Landfilling. Exhibit 1-19 provides the net emission factor for landfilling glass.
